export default {"G000109":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · structure · <code>G000109</code></p><h3>Big affine fppf site of a scheme</h3><p>Take the full subcategory of the big fppf site over <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> on those <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U\\to S</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> for which <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is affine. Use finite jointly surjective families of flat, locally finitely presented morphisms from affine schemes as standard fppf covers.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/021S\">Stacks 021S · big affine fppf site · Stacks 021S · common source definition · Stacks 021S · Item 2 · big affine site</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topologies/#tag-021S\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000109\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000114":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · predicate · <code>G000114</code></p><h3>Bounded prism</h3><p>A prism <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(A,I)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is bounded if there is an integer <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\geq0</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> such that <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p^n(A/I)[p^\\infty]=0</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.4007/annals.2022.196.3.5\">Bhatt–Scholze, Prisms and prismatic cohomology, Definition 1.1</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000114\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000101":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · construction · <code>G000101</code></p><h3>Covering-family presentation</h3><p>A category with specified families of arrows <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>→</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\{U_i\\to U\\}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> containing the isomorphism covers, closed under composition of covers, and stable under base change along every arrow to a covering target. The requisite pullbacks of the covering arrows exist.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VH\">Stacks 00VH · site specified by covering families · Stacks 00VH · common source definition · Stacks 00VH · covering-family presentation of a site</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00VH\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000101\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000116":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · predicate · <code>G000116</code></p><h3>Effective hypercover</h3><p>A hypercover <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∙</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U_\\bullet</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is effective if its colimit in <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal X_{/V}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is terminal; equivalently the augmentation induces an equivalence <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∙</mo></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mo>≃</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|U_\\bullet|\\simeq V</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> in <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://www.math.ias.edu/~lurie/papers/HTT.pdf#page=693\">Lurie, Higher Topos Theory, Definition 6.5.3.2, applied in the slice</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000116\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000107":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · construction · <code>G000107</code></p><h3>Enough points</h3><p>A family of points is conservative if a map of sheaves is an isomorphism whenever the induced map at every stalk in the family is bijective. A site has enough points when it admits a conservative family of points.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Y5\">Stacks 00Y5 · point of a site</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00Y5\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00YK\">Stacks 00YK · conservative family of points · Stacks 00YK · common source definition · Stacks 00YK · (2) existence of a conservative family</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00YK\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000107\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000115":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · structure · <code>G000115</code></p><h3>Frame</h3><p>A frame is a complete lattice in which finite meets distribute over arbitrary joins. Frame homomorphisms preserve finite meets and arbitrary joins.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://dml.cz/handle/10338.dmlcz/118836\">Banaschewski, Radical ideals and coherent frames, §1</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000115\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000106":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · construction · <code>G000106</code></p><h3>Geometric morphism</h3><p>A morphism <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">ℰ</mi><mo>→</mo><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f:\\mathcal E\\to\\mathcal F</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> of topoi is an adjunction <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>:</mo><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">ℱ</mi><mo>⇄</mo><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">ℰ</mi><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f^{-1}:\\mathcal F\\rightleftarrows\\mathcal E:f_*</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> with <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> left adjoint and preserving finite limits.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00XA\">Stacks 00XA · morphism of topoi · Stacks 00XA · common source definition · Stacks 00XA · Item 1 · adjunction between inverse image and direct image · Stacks 00XA · Item 1 · preservation of finite limits by inverse image</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00XA\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000106\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000103":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · structure · <code>G000103</code></p><h3>Grothendieck topology in sieves</h3><p>For each object <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> choose a collection <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J(U)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> of covering sieves. It contains <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h_U</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and is stable under pullback. If <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S\\in J(U)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and a sieve <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> restricts to a covering sieve along every arrow in <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, then <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R\\in J(U)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. A sheaf <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> satisfies <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≅</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Hom</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F(U)\\cong\\operatorname{Hom}(S,F)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> by restriction for each <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S\\in J(U)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z4\">Stacks 00Z4 · topology axioms · Stacks 00Z4 · common source definition · Stacks 00Z4 · Grothendieck topology on sieves</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00Z4\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z8\">Stacks 00Z8 · sheaf condition for covering sieves</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00Z8\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000103\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000112":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · predicate · <code>G000112</code></p><h3>Hypercomplete ∞-topos</h3><p>An ∞-topos <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is hypercomplete if every ∞-connective morphism in <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is an equivalence.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://www.math.ias.edu/~lurie/papers/HTT.pdf#page=687\">Lurie, Higher Topos Theory, §6.5.2</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000112\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000111":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · predicate · <code>G000111</code></p><h3>Hypercomplete object</h3><p>An object <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Z</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is hypercomplete if for every ∞-connective morphism <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f:A\\to B</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, precomposition gives an equivalence <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Map</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≃</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Map</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Map}(B,Z)\\simeq\\operatorname{Map}(A,Z)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://www.math.ias.edu/~lurie/papers/HTT.pdf#page=687\">Lurie, Higher Topos Theory, §6.5.2</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000111\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000110":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · construction · <code>G000110</code></p><h3>Hypercompletion</h3><p>For an ∞-topos <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, form the accessible left exact localization at its ∞-connective morphisms. The resulting full reflective subcategory <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒳</mi><mo>∧</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal X^\\wedge</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> consists of objects local with respect to those morphisms.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://www.math.ias.edu/~lurie/papers/HTT.pdf#page=687\">Lurie, Higher Topos Theory, §6.5.2</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000110\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000113":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · structure · <code>G000113</code></p><h3>Hypercover</h3><p>A simplicial object <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∙</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U_\\bullet</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> in <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal X_{/V}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is a hypercover of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> when for each <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\geq0</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> the map <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>→</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cosk</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∙</mo></msub><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U_n\\to(\\operatorname{cosk}_{n-1}U_\\bullet)_n</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is an effective epimorphism in the slice. In degree zero the matching object is the terminal object <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> of the slice.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://www.math.ias.edu/~lurie/papers/HTT.pdf#page=693\">Lurie, Higher Topos Theory, Definition 6.5.3.2, applied in the slice</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000113\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000100":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · construction · <code>G000100</code></p><h3>Prime spectrum of a ring</h3><p>For a commutative ring <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, the points of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Spec}(A)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> are prime ideals. The principal opens <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">𝔭</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>f</mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\">∉</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">𝔭</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D(f)=\\{\\mathfrak p:f\\notin\\mathfrak p\\}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> form a basis of the Zariski topology.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00DY\">Stacks 00DY · the spectrum of a ring</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00DY\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9947-1969-0251026-X\">Hochster, Prime ideal structure in commutative rings, Theorem 6</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00DZ\">Stacks 00DZ · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00DZ\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000100\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000104":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · construction · <code>G000104</code></p><h3>Sheafification</h3><p>The left adjoint <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>↦</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">#</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F\\mapsto F^\\#</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> to the inclusion of sheaves of sets in presheaves. It can be computed by applying the plus construction twice. The plus construction forms the colimit, over refinements, of matching families on covers.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00WH\">Stacks 00WH · sheafification on a site</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00WH\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00ZM\">Stacks 00ZM · sheafification for a topology in sieves</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00ZM\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00ZL\">Stacks 00ZL · double plus together with its unit</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00ZL\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00WG\">Stacks 00WG · double family plus and its unit</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00WG\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000104\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000102":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · construction · <code>G000102</code></p><h3>Sieve on an object</h3><p>A sieve on <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is a subpresheaf <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S\\subseteq h_U</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> of the representable presheaf. Equivalently its arrows with target <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> are closed under precomposition. The pullback along <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V\\to U</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><msub><mo>×</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S\\times_{h_U}h_V\\subseteq h_V</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00YX\">Stacks 00YX · sieve · Stacks 00YX · subpresheaf of the represented object</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00YX\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z2\">Stacks 00Z2 · pullback of a sieve</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00Z2\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000102\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000105":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · predicate · <code>G000105</code></p><h3>Subcanonical topology</h3><p>A Grothendieck topology <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> on <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal C</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is subcanonical if, for every object <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi class=\"math-euler-script\" mathvariant=\"normal\">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal C</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, the representable presheaf <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h_U</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is a <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">J</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>-sheaf.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00WQ\">Stacks 00WQ · subcanonical site · Stacks 00WQ · all covering families are universally effective epimorphic</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-00WQ\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000105\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000108":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Sites and presentations · construction · <code>G000108</code></p><h3>Weakly contractible object of a site</h3><p>An object <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is weakly contractible if evaluation at <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> sends epimorphisms of sheaves of sets to surjections. Equivalently the canonical map <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∐</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">#</mi></msubsup><mo>→</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">#</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\coprod_i h_{U_i}^\\#\\to h_U^\\#</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> in sheaves admits a section for every covering <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>→</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\{U_i\\to U\\}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/090K\">Stacks 090K · equivalent criteria for weak contractibility</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-090K\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/090L\">Stacks 090L · enough weakly contractible objects · Stacks 090L · common source definition · Stacks 090L · (1) weakly contractible object</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/sites/#tag-090L\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000108\">Open shared record</a></p></article>","G000159":"<article class=\"algebra-definition atlas-panel\"><p class=\"property-context\">Commutative rings · construction · <code>G000159</code></p><h3>Zariski topology on a prime spectrum</h3><p>The closed sets of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Spec}R</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> are the subsets <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V(T)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> as <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> ranges over subsets of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. Their complements are unions of standard opens.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00E1\">Stacks 00E1 · numbered source · Stacks 00E1 · common source definition</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/algebra/#tag-00E1\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"../database/#G000159\">Open shared record</a></p></article>"};
